  "review_notes": [
    "Reconciliation: the supplied *for* moved from מֵאָה to the verb יוֹתֵר under rule 33's direct-object paragraph and rule 44's supplied-preposition clause; the numeral keeps *a hundred* under rule 15. Competing reading: *for* on the numeral as a purpose relation the ASV chose (rule 33's first sentence) — rejected because only what governs the noun in the Hebrew decides it, and the hiphil governs מֵאָה רָכֶב as its object."
